<section>
<h2>Lists</h2>
<ul>
<li>No manual bullets (-, °, *)</li>
<li>If there is only one item in the list, it isn't a list</li>
<li>Navigation menu's usually are lists</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section>
<h2>Tables</h2>
<ul>
<li>th elements for table headings</li>
<li>caption for the legend (if present)</li>
<li><a target="tweede" href="https://examples.anysurfer.be/2.4.2/table_headings.html">example</a></li>
<li><a href="http://examples.anysurfer.be/2.4.2/table_to_be_corrected.html">Exercise: inspect and correct</a></li>
</ul>
</section>


		<section>
			<h2>HTML5 - sectioning elements </h2>
			<ul>
				<li><code is:raw>header</code> and <code is:raw>footer</code></li>
				<li><code is:raw>main</code> for main content</li>
				<li><code is:raw>nav</code> for important navigation sections</li>
				<li><code is:raw>article</code> only for blocs that can be read independently</li>
				<li><code is:raw>aside</code> for secondary info</li>				
			</ul>
			  <aside class="notes"><p>If the page is correctly divided into regions (header, main, footer, nav,...) assistive technology can use this information to offer shortcuts to the users. These elements should be used according to the specification and there should not be too many of them. Having a couple of navigation regions helps navigationg the page but if there are too many, they are not so useful any more.  </p></aside>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>Don't misuse semantic elements</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>No h6 for small paragraph of text</li>
				<li>No blockquote just to indent some content</li>
				<li>Nav only for main navigation regions (don't overdo it)</li>
			</ul>
		</section>
		<section>
            <h2>Exercise: identify the structure of a page</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Pick a page on a website</li>
                    <li>Observe the page without looking at the code</li>
                    <li>Identify the regions: header, main, footer, nav </li>
                    <li>Identify the headings and their levels </li>
                </ul>
       </section>


          <section>
          <h2>Do not use text for visual effects</h2>

                        <pre><code is:raw>HH   HH        lll lll
HH   HH   eee  lll lll  oooo
HHHHHHH ee   e lll lll oo  oo
HH   HH eeeee  lll lll oo  oo
HH   HH  eeeee lll lll  oooo


        (\___/)
        (='.'=)
        ( U U )
        (")_(")</code></pre>
          <aside class="notes"><p>This is unreadable with a screenreader.  </p></aside>
                    </section>


		<section>	
			<h2>Do not use text for visual effects</h2>						
			<ul>
				<li>Use "next" and "previous" instead of "">>" and "&lt;&lt;" </li>
				<li>Avoid ascii art and leetspeak</li>
				<li>Use css to add space between letters and between paragraphs</li>
			</ul>
		</section>
	</section>
